# Tech stack — SvelteKit app

**`src/`** is SvelteKit 2 + Svelte 5. Do not reintroduce Next.js or client React.

## Use

- SvelteKit file routes (`+page.svelte`, `+page.server.ts`, `+server.ts`)
- Svelte 5 runes (`$state`, `$derived`, `.svelte.ts` stores)
- shadcn-svelte + Bits UI
- sveltekit-superforms + Zod
- Charts: SVG donuts; CSS ranking tracks for investor capital; ApexCharts only for cashflow. Not Recharts.
- lucide-svelte for icons
- Drizzle + Neon (server-only)
- `@auth/sveltekit`

## Ban in src/

| Banned | Why |
| ------ | --- |
| `next/*`, `next-auth` | Legacy stack |
| Client React, Radix React, Recharts | Use Svelte equivalents |
| `react-hook-form`, `zustand` | Use superforms + runes |
| tRPC, Supabase client patterns | Wrong stack |

## Allowed exception

Server-only `@react-pdf/renderer` for PDF exports (`pdf-export` skill). React must not ship to the browser bundle.
